    "title": "Jimmy Kimmel Wins! - NewsBreak",
    "text": "19 days ago We did it, Joe Jim. Nexstar will be following Sinclair’s lead and bringing Jimmy Kimmel Live! back to its airwaves. “Nexstar today announced that Jimmy Kimmel Live! will return to the company’s owned and partner television stations affiliated with the ABC Television Network beginning tonight,” it said in a statement, albeit one that ignores the fact that tonight’s JKL! is technically a rerun. Luckily for those in Nexstar markets like Wheeling, West Virginia, and Steubenville, Ohio, the episode that will run tonight is a repeat of Tuesday’s record-breaking first episode back from suspension. Revel in Kimmel’s monologue, Steubenville. Then learn that the JKL! producers used to let an out-of-work Glen Powell rummage through their greenroom leftovers like some sort of telegenic raccoon. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
